 "title": "Present tense, verbs in -ώ (αγαπώ, θεωρώ)",
 "section": "A1 · Holton §6.9-6.10",
 "goal": "Conjugate both types of stress-final verbs in the present.",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "Verbs stressed on the final -ώ form the **second conjugation**, and the stress always sits on the ending. They split into two types by the vowel that dominates the endings:\n\n**Type A** (α-type): αγαπώ, μιλώ, ρωτώ, ξεχνώ, περνώ, πουλώ, σταματώ. Many have doublets in -άω (αγαπάω, μιλάω), which are slightly more colloquial and equally correct.\n\n**Type B** (ει/ου-type): θεωρώ, μπορώ, προσπαθώ, παρακαλώ, αποτελώ. Fewer verbs, often more learned, but μπορώ is among the most common verbs in the language."
  },
  {
   "type": "verb-paradigm",
   "columns": [
