  },
  {
   "type": "culture",
   "title": "Παρακαλώ, the all-purpose verb",
   "text": "**Παρακαλώ**, a type B verb literally 'I request', is one of the most useful words in Greek. It means 'please' (**Ένα νερό, παρακαλώ**), 'you're welcome' in reply to ευχαριστώ, and, said as a question, **Παρακαλώ;** 'Can I help you?' in a shop or 'Hello?' when answering the phone. Other phone openers are **Ναι;**, **Λέγετε** 'Go ahead' and the old-fashioned **Εμπρός**. Its partner **Ορίστε** 'here you are' also answers the phone or asks 'Pardon?'."
  },
